ered":7249,"medianLagDays":1222}]},"findings":[{"sev":"alert","title":"Australian patenting fell while foreign filing 2.4×'d","body":"Australian-origin patent applications went from 8,897 in 1995 to 6,570 in 2023 — a fall in absolute terms, not just in share. Over the same years foreign filings into Australia rose from 12,467 to 29,380 — a factor of 2.36. The Australian share of all patent filings dropped from 41.6% to 18.3%.","view":"divergence"},{"sev":"info","title":"Australians brand far more readily than they invent","body":"In 2023, 58% of trade mark applications came from Australian applicants, against just 18.3% of patent applications. Australia registers its own brands and imports its inventions.","view":"divergence"},{"sev":"info","title":"Australia's most prolific filer is Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organisation","body":"Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organisation has filed 7,609 applications since 1955, ahead of Aristocrat Technologies Australia Pty Limited (6,950). Filer groups merge registered-name variants — open a row to see exactly which names were combined.","view":"filers"},{"sev":"info","title":"Five countries supply 66.7% of all foreign filing","body":"United States of America, United Kingdom, China, Germany, Japan together account for 1,264,868 of the 1,895,236 applications filed here by an applicant outside Australia, across 232 countries in total.","view":"origin"},{"sev":"warn","title":"The innovation patent is gone, and the data shows exactly when","body":"Innovation patents peaked at 7,833 filings in 2021. They were closed to new applications on 26 August 2021, and only 347 appear across 2023 onward. This cliff is legislative, not behavioural.","view":"lifecycle"}]}